A minimal class that ties state, a constructor enforcing a valid starting point, and behavior together:

```java
class BankAccount {
    private double balance;

    BankAccount(double openingBalance) {
        this.balance = openingBalance;
    }

    void deposit(double amount) {
        this.balance += amount;
    }

    double getBalance() {
        return this.balance;
    }
}

BankAccount acc = new BankAccount(100.0);
acc.deposit(50.0);
System.out.println(acc.getBalance()); // 150.0
```

Notice what each piece buys you: `private` hides `balance` from direct access (state), the constructor guarantees every account starts with a real balance instead of `0` by accident (initialization), and `deposit` is the only sanctioned way to change it (behavior).
